  "worked_solution": "The first four terms of the series are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =x \\\\ {a}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3} \\\\ {a}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{7}{x}^{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we can express these terms using a common format, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{{x}^{2\\cdot 0+1}}{2\\cdot 0+1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =\\frac{{x}^{2\\cdot 1+1}}{2\\cdot 1+1} \\\\ {a}_{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2\\cdot 2+1}}{2\\cdot 2+1} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =\\frac{{x}^{2\\cdot 3+1}}{2\\cdot 3+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe deduce that the general formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{{x}^{2n+1}}{2n+1}\\,.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}\u2061\\sqrt{\\frac{1+x}{1-x}}={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2n+1}}{2n+1}.\n$$",
